Note with the Company&#8217;s new capital structure and intercreditor arrangements. The revised agreement extended the maturity of the Second Lien Note to March 30, 2026. At the option of the Company, the maturity of the Second Lien Note was further extended to September 30, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The obligations under the Second Lien Note are fully and unconditionally guaranteed by certain subsidiaries of BPA and are secured by liens on BPA&#8217;s and certain guarantors&#8217; assets, including accounts receivable, inventory, cash and deposit accounts, equipment, real property, equity interests in subsidiaries, intercompany obligations, general intangibles, and other related assets. Pursuant to the ABL Intercreditor Agreement, BRF Finance Co., LLC&#8217;s liens are subordinated to the liens securing the Company&#8217;s senior debt facilities; specifically, the ABL Facility with respect to receivables, inventory, cash, and related assets, and the Super Senior Term Loan and July 2030 Notes with respect to fixed assets, equity interests, and other non-ABL assets. As a result, the obligations under the Second Lien Note are effectively second-priority liens behind the senior secured debt. The Second Lien Notes requires the borrowers to maintain a minimum fixed charge coverage ratio, calculated on a trailing twelve-month basis. The minimum required ratio varies depending on the period: for the defined periods tested quarterly through December 31, 2025, and monthly from January 1, 2026, through June 30, 2026, the fixed charge coverage ratio must be not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_x-DraIrURkqybk-ATSvGbg" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_DefinedPeriodTestedQuarterlyThroughDecember312025AndMonthlyFromJanuary12026ThroughJune302026Member_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_rtafrRi8Z0eJpRp-lUmMdA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_yoXLpgYdSkClUiOE6VkSCg">0.85</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00. Thereafter, for the defined periods tested monthly from July 1, 2026, through the maturity date, the fixed charge coverage ratio must be not less than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_x-DraIrURkqybk-ATSvGbg" contextRef="As_Of_7_29_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xbp_DefinedPeriodsTestedMonthlyFromJuly12026ThroughMaturityDateMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_DXYIy0XTDECwTtCTXiuU5g" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xbp:DebtInstrumentCovenantMinimumFixedChargeCoverageRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_imvo2dQaOEeDcrh97v1OCw">1.00</ix:nonFraction> to 1.00. The Company was in compliance with all financial covenants as of December 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">During 2024 (Predecessor), the Company had repaid $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_q4HVJlM7Q0StRndL3BeWvQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_lUoUtMqw3kWGvTMzH7OgNg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfLongTermDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_zvhs11SJwUauHeLJAJgfCg">6.0</ix:nonFraction> million principal amount of the Second Lien Note. The loss on early extinguishment of the debt during the year ended December 31, 2024 (Predecessor) totaled $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_q4HVJlM7Q0StRndL3BeWvQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_lUoUtMqw3kWGvTMzH7OgNg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GainsLossesOnExtinguishmentOfDebt" scale="6" id="Narr_O9ML4y_CmU23GwbFegSWCA">0.4</ix:nonFraction> million and is inclusive of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_q4HVJlM7Q0StRndL3BeWvQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_xbp_SecondLienSecuredTermLoanMember_lUoUtMqw3kWGvTMzH7OgNg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:WriteOffOfDeferredDebtIssuanceCost" scale="6" id="Narr_J58y3IEXjkSg8tgByFs9Sg">0.4</ix:nonFraction> million write off of debt issuance costs. As of December 31, 2024 (Predecessor), there </p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">113</p></div></div>
